+# HANDOFF — html-to-editable-pptx parser (rule-based)
+
+Status date: 2026-06-12 · Sessions completed: 3 · All validation gates GREEN.
+This packet is self-contained: no prior conversation context is required.
+
+> Provenance note (integration): this document is the original h2p handoff,
+> imported verbatim except for path updates (`src/map/` → `src/mapper/`,
+> `vendor/dom-to-pptx/` → `third_party/subtrees/dom-to-pptx/`). It records the
+> state of the working pipeline at the moment it was merged into
+> `goodand/html-to-editable-pptx`. See `docs/h2p_integration_work_order_v0.1.md`.
+
+## 1. Mission and policy
+
+Build an editability-first HTML→PPTX parser. Every recoverable element becomes a
+native, editable PowerPoint object — never a screenshot.
+
+Action priority (highest first): consistency with intent > completion > fast user
+verification > re-reading > reusability > reuse existing > validation > read >
+optimization > copy > deletion > create new.
+
+Hard constraints:
+- **Rule-based only.** No LLM, no multimodal model, no ML at any stage. Same
+  input → byte-identical output, every run.
+- **Reuse before writing.** Sources: `third_party/subtrees/dom-to-pptx` (ideas + one file
+  imported verbatim), the diff-parser mechanisms (bag-of-lines, MD5, Jaccard —
+  already absorbed into `src/validate/`), PptxGenJS/pixelmatch as npm deps.
+- Patch line-by-line (`str_replace`-style edits); read files before editing.
+
+## 2. What exists and works
+
+Pipeline (all implemented, all green on `fixtures/deck.html`, 3 slides / 19 nodes):
+
+```
+HTML ──weasy_extract.py──▶ IR v1.2.0 ──ir_to_pptx.mjs──▶ .pptx
+        (WeasyPrint box tree)   │            (PptxGenJS + subtree normalizer)
+                                └─ masks.json (chart regions for Layer C)
+Validation (run.sh, parallel subflows):
+  Layer A semantic   bag-of-lines + per-slide Jaccard   → missing 0, jaccard 1.0
+  Layer B binary     MD5 media hashing                  → 1/1 matched
+  Layer C visual     pixelmatch, chart bboxes masked    → 3.09 / 1.19 / 1.26 %  (<5 gate)
+  Layer D geometric  IR bbox vs OOXML xfrm IoU          → 19/19 ok, worstIoU 0.996
+  Editability        native objects / total             → 1.0 (19/19, 0 fallback)
+```
+
+Capabilities: multi-slide (`<section class="slide">` + page breaks), tables with
+colspan/rowspan (WeasyPrint `grid_x/colspan/rowspan` attrs), opacity (ancestor
+product → transparency), overflow:hidden clipping (bbox intersection), images
+(MD5-tracked), charts via two rule-based tiers — tier1 `data-*` JSON attrs
+(source-first), tier2 SVG mark + numeric-axis-tick linear scale reverse
+engineering. Unparseable SVG → `fallbackRegion` with reason, never silent.
+
+## 3. Directory map
+
+```
+├── run.sh                  # orchestrator: extract → map → ∥(A+B | render) → C per page → D
+├── setup_mac.sh            # macOS bootstrap (brew poppler/pango/libreoffice, pip weasyprint, npm ci)
+├── package.json / -lock    # pptxgenjs, pixelmatch, pngjs, jszip, @xmldom/xmldom
+├── src/
+│   ├── ir/schema.ts        # IR CONTRACT v1.2.0 — invariants I1–I9 (read first)
+│   ├── ir/validate.js      # runtime validator; mapper refuses invalid IR
+│   ├── extract/weasy_extract.py  # HTML→IR; probe-hardened walk (see §5 footguns)
+│   ├── mapper/ir_to_pptx.mjs  # IR→PPTX; imports subtree normalizer via DOMParser polyfill
+│   └── validate/
+│       ├── validate_ab.py  # Layers A+B (svg blocks excluded from A)
+│       ├── pixel_c.mjs     # Layer C with mask support
+│       └── layout_d.py     # Layer D per-object IoU, sourceRef-addressed report
+├── fixtures/deck.html      # 3-slide acceptance fixture (spans/opacity/clip/charts)
+├── fixtures/slide13.html   # original single-slide fixture
+├── docs/lessons.md         # numbered lessons — REQUIRED READING before editing
+├── third_party/subtrees/dom-to-pptx/  # MIT; only src/pptx-normalizer.js is imported at runtime
+└── out/                    # generated artifacts (see §6)
+```
+
+## 4. How to run
+
+Linux container: deps preinstalled pattern — `pip install weasyprint
+--break-system-packages`, `npm ci`, fonts-noto-cjk, poppler-utils, LibreOffice.
+macOS: `bash setup_mac.sh` once.
+
+```
+bash run.sh fixtures/deck.html
+```
+
+Pass criteria (machine-checkable):
+- `out/deck.ab.json` → `layerA_semantic.pass: true`, every slide `jaccard: 1.0`,
+  `layerB_media.pass: true`
+- stage-4 stdout → each slide `diffPct < 5`
+- `out/deck.d.json` → `layerD_layout.pass: true`, `worstIoU > 0.90`
+- `out/deck.mapreport.json` → `editabilityScore: 1`, `fallback: 0`
+
+## 5. Footguns (violating these caused every bug so far)
+
+1. **Unwrap before classifying.** WeasyPrint wraps absolute-positioned boxes in
+   `AbsolutePlaceholder`; `__getattr__` delegates to `._box`, so class checks
+   pass-through silently. Always `getattr(box, "_box", box)` first.
+2. **Rows are never direct children.** Implicit `TableRowGroupBox` (tbody) sits
+   between `TableBox` and rows — collect recursively.
+3. **Tags can be namespaced.** Inline SVG tag is `{http://...}svg` — match with
+   `tag.endswith("svg")`.
+4. **Style keys drift by version.** v69 renamed `text_align`→`text_align_all`;
+   wrap style reads in try/except.
+5. **Always pass `h:` to addTable.** PptxGenJS defaults graphicFrame `cy` to
+   1 inch; renderers auto-repair so pixel/visual QA pass while the declaration
+   is wrong. Only Layer D catches this class.
+6. **Provenance comes from raw HTML, not the box tree.** Image srcs and chart
+   data are collected by a second stdlib parse, joined by document-order queues.
+   Assumption: traversal order == document order (breaks under CSS reordering).
+
+Companion skill: `skills/software-development/cross-representation-verification/SKILL.md`
+(probe-first / dual-source / declaration-level validation) generalizes these.
+
+## 6. Artifact inventory (out/)
+
+| File | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `deck.ir.json` | IR v1.2.0 — slides[].nodes[], the contract instance |
+| `deck.masks.json` | per-slide chart bboxes excluded from Layer C |
+| `deck.pptx` | final deliverable (normalizer-passed, 0 dangling overrides) |
+| `deck.mapreport.json` | node counts, editabilityScore, fallback log |
+| `deck.ab.json` / `deck.d.json` | Layer A+B / Layer D reports |
+| `deck_A-N.png` / `deck_B-N.png` / `deck_diff-N.png` | source render / output render / pixel diff per slide |
+
+## 7. Pending roadmap (priority order)
+
+1. **L4 render-environment pinning** — Docker image pinning fonts-noto-cjk +
+   LibreOffice version; only then tighten Layer C below 5% (cross-renderer font
+   rasterization floor ≈ 2.85%). Blocked in the build container; viable locally.
+2. **CSS z-index** — extractor currently uses DOM paint order only; port
+   dom-to-pptx `sortKey = parent.concat([zVal, order])` composite-key idea.
+3. **Border-radius clipping** — clip stack intersects rectangles only; rounded
+   clips are approximated as rectangular.
+4. **Chart breadth** — line/pie detection (circle/path marks), multi-series
+   (color-grouped rects), legend extraction; keep the two-tier ladder.
+5. **Crop-fallback for unrecoverable SVG** — render source page once, crop the
+   fallbackRegion bbox into an asset-backed image instead of dropping visuals.
+6. **Text transparency check** — `transparency` is passed on addText; verify
+   OOXML alpha lands on text runs across PowerPoint versions (works in LO).
+
+## 8. Verification-first start procedure for the next agent
+
+1. Read `docs/lessons.md`, then `src/ir/schema.ts` (I1–I9).
+2. Run `bash run.sh fixtures/deck.html`; confirm §4 pass criteria before any edit.
+3. Any new element type: write a minimal fixture, PROBE the box tree, then a
+   handler, then extend `fixtures/deck.html` and re-run all four layers.
+4. Record every correction in `docs/lessons.md` (numbered, one-line summary first).
